EXT. ROOFTOP FIVES COURT, COPENHAGEN - DUSK

A tarred roof above a canal. A white-painted court on the asphalt, four walls of corrugated steel. Chimney pots and TV aerials ring the horizon. Down in the water, a barge horn moans.

ASTRID LUNDGAARD, 40s, silver braid, plays barefoot, gloved hand hitting a hard rubber ball. Across from her, MATEUSZ KRÓL, 30s, shirtless, a tattoo of a swallow across his ribs. In the corner, with a stopwatch and a radio headset, THANDI MOKOENA, 20s, referee, jots numbers on her palm.

Astrid slams a backhand. The ball cracks off the steel and Mateusz dives, scrapes his knee, returns it high, and Astrid follows it back with a lunge and a swing, and he counters with a lob that lands in the corner, while Thandi shouts the score into her headset.

THANDI
(to the whole roof)
Eleven all! Next point takes the set!

RADIO (V.O.)
(tinny, from the headset)
Copy, referee. Broadcast is live. Keep it moving.

MATEUSZ
(muttering)
Live. Everything's live. Nothing's alive.

ASTRID
(to Mateusz)
You're drifting left.

MATEUSZ
You always say that.

ASTRID
Because you always drift.

They set. Astrid serves, a vicious spinning shot. Mateusz reads it, steps in, volleys. They rally, long, ferocious. Thandi counts.

THANDI
(to herself)
Please don't go to twelve.

ASTRID
(to Thandi)
Girl, hush. Let us breathe.

The ball skims the tape and drops. A held breath. Astrid and Mateusz stare at where it died.

THANDI
(to the whole roof)
Point, Lundgaard! Set to Lundgaard!

Mateusz drops to a knee, panting. Astrid walks to him, extends a gloved hand. He takes it. Down on the canal, the barge horn sounds again, longer this time.
